('d4914e59-28c6-5510-993e-7708b06e344d','0e7c1bfe-5aa3-53b0-af21-9a36ff054b3d',6,'Serve warm, with the filling of your choice.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('93b57337-efac-5a79-b441-c33e6244a7ab','b93e71ab-3d41-5dd4-88c4-5bba38702cae',1,'Soak herring in cold water for at least 1 hour. If very salty, repeat, changing the water each time.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('bed17ef8-792a-5895-b196-0a2eff8faedc','b93e71ab-3d41-5dd4-88c4-5bba38702cae',2,'Drain thoroughly and slice herring into bite-size pieces.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a3902b5f-22b7-5ad3-a84b-e7cb50d24364','b93e71ab-3d41-5dd4-88c4-5bba38702cae',3,'Place in a jar large enough to accommodate the pieces and cover with oil, allspice, peppercorns, and bay leaf. Close the jar.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('fd591646-7042-5e12-8668-db204409381e','b93e71ab-3d41-5dd4-88c4-5bba38702cae',4,'Refrigerate for 2 to 3 days before eating. This will keep refrigerated up to 2 weeks.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('eb118ed2-27f4-5f98-9612-d3a8563bfaa8','b93e71ab-3d41-5dd4-88c4-5bba38702cae',5,'Serve with finely chopped onion or onion slices, lemon, and parsley or dill.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9ae9e7f9-9c29-57f4-844a-3901ae66391b','6654dc58-5579-5c09-ac46-3b9c7257391f',1,'As the cooking time varies depending on the quality and age of the beans, it is good to cook them in advance and to reheat them when you are ready to serve. Cook the drained beans in a fresh portion of unsalted water in a large saucepan with the lid on until tender, adding water to keep them covered, and salt when the beans have softened. They take 2–2 1/2 hours of gentle simmering. When the beans are soft, let the liquid reduce. It is usual to take out a ladle or two of the beans and to mash them with some of the cooking liquid, then stir this back into the beans. This is to thicken the sauce.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('3cdd324a-b49b-5fb7-8fb0-cb116f30f347','6654dc58-5579-5c09-ac46-3b9c7257391f',2,'Serve the beans in soup bowls sprinkled with chopped parsley and accompanied by Arab bread.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('dc5d6da2-7deb-5ec4-947d-70d66019561b','6654dc58-5579-5c09-ac46-3b9c7257391f',3,'Pass round the dressing ingredients for everyone to help themselves: a bottle of extra-virgin olive oil, the quartered lemons, salt and pepper, a little saucer with the crushed garlic, one with chili-pepper flakes, and one with ground cumin.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
