('b16f7b61-9d78-5d58-bd0a-e2a37d2a02da','fd7398a9-62e6-5eaf-adbf-663bd7c3887e',1,'Tip the bread into a bowl and pour over 350ml water. Leave to soak for 10 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('dbecd952-1d2c-5824-b7c4-7bd37a7bb7a9','fd7398a9-62e6-5eaf-adbf-663bd7c3887e',2,'Blend the ingredients together with 350ml water and 1 tsp salt.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('105b6386-21a0-5bb3-949b-c9dc3f55e15c','fd7398a9-62e6-5eaf-adbf-663bd7c3887e',3,'Let the soup cool in the fridge for 1 hr or so, then serve with a drizzle of oil and some black pepper.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('669f552d-67d8-541c-afc2-78731fb71d81','7c0871ee-1f1b-5165-8190-138cb9794c6f',1,'Heat half the oil in a frying pan, and sauté the onion over a medium heat until soft and pale gold – this will take about 8 mins. Remove from the pan, set aside, and add the potatoes to the pan. Cook until they are tender but not falling apart, carefully turning every so often. Cover the pan some of the time to help the slices cook through. Add the onions back to the pan along with the garlic and cook for another 4 mins. Tip into a bowl with the eggs, parsley and some seasoning and mix together. Leave to sit for half an hour.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('27395b04-d2fe-5056-9720-5bb39e09779f','7c0871ee-1f1b-5165-8190-138cb9794c6f',2,'Meanwhile, put the cod in a saucepan and cover with water. Bring up to a simmer. Remove from the heat, cover and leave for 10 mins. Drain, leave to cool and remove the skin and any bones. Break into large flakes and add to the potato and egg mixture.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('66c402f5-2baa-550e-b813-5cc3cd8ec8b0','7c0871ee-1f1b-5165-8190-138cb9794c6f',3,'Heat the rest of the oil in a non-stick frying pan. Pour in the tortilla mix and cook over a medium-low heat until it is just set and coming away from the sides of the pan. You might need to cover it to help the centre set. Be careful not to overcook it. Put a spatula underneath the tortilla every so often to make sure it isn’t sticking. Slide the tortilla onto a plate, then put the pan on top and flip the tortilla into it, uncooked side-down. Cook over a low heat until golden, or grill until just set. Leave to cool a little before serving.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('5a811ebe-ec41-5520-b7ba-b61b5a65cf71','6ced9317-e57a-59d3-81ab-a4a608754b4f',1,'Heat the oil in a pan and fry the onion for about 5 mins until softened. Add the garlic, chopped tomatoes, tomato purée, sweet paprika, chilli powder, sugar and a pinch of salt, then bring to the boil, stirring occasionally. Lower to a simmer and cook for 10 mins until pulpy. Can be kept chilled for up to 24 hrs.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4295b095-5370-5965-b616-c8eac287ede4','6ced9317-e57a-59d3-81ab-a4a608754b4f',2,'Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Pat the potatoes dry with kitchen paper, then tip into a roasting tin and toss in the olive oil and some seasoning. Roast for 40-50 mins until crisp and golden. Tip the potatoes into serving dishes and spoon over the tomato sauce. Sprinkle with some fresh parsley to serve.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6deb93e0-9df6-5071-bb8b-aaa9f06c6ce8','f69f934e-b75b-5d70-a7d5-f260e7153899',1,'Put a pan of water on over a high heat to boil. Meanwhile, snip the chorizo into strips with scissors, and chop the parsley and peppers (check for stray seeds first).',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('941d9724-8876-5121-b099-6017072e3dde','f69f934e-b75b-5d70-a7d5-f260e7153899',2,'When the water is boiling briskly, add the spaghetti with a good measure of salt, stir and return to the boil. Cook for 3 minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7b73654e-4fb2-54b2-8dfb-045b9d4da102','f69f934e-b75b-5d70-a7d5-f260e7153899',3,'In a large frying pan, heat the oil, add the chorizo and peppers and plenty of black pepper. Cook for a minute or so, until heated through and the juices are stained red from the paprika in the chorizo. Scoop half a mugful of pasta water from the pan, drain the remainder and tip the spaghetti into the frying pan.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a53258ab-c5e4-55ab-b37e-0b87b12515f1','f69f934e-b75b-5d70-a7d5-f260e7153899',4,'Add the parsley and parmesan, toss well and splash in the pasta water, to moisten. Hand round extra parmesan at the table.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('3f399bdc-e8a9-5773-8e96-ca6d42fd4db9','eb8977bc-89ac-5843-a8f9-ce49929bd8de',1,'Heat the olive oil in a large frying pan. Tip in the garlic slices and cook for a few secs. Then stir through the prawns and cook for a couple of mins until they start to turn pink.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('bad954ec-cf8b-5eae-a360-8344834010b9','eb8977bc-89ac-5843-a8f9-ce49929bd8de',2,'Pour over the sherry and cook for a few mins more, just until the prawns are cooked through. Sprinkle with parsley before serving.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('742d5f5b-891c-5e6b-8627-d665c54290f1','b4e9cab4-296d-5d77-8584-fa273daa32a6',1,'Soak the beans for at least 4 hrs or overnight in a large bowl with plenty of water to cover. Next day, rinse and drain, then put in a large heavy based pan with the onion, paprika, herb bundle and chicken. Pour over enough water or stock to cover, bring to the boil, then reduce the heat, cover and simmer for 45 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('dcb345e4-a103-54c8-9675-217b7d655350','b4e9cab4-296d-5d77-8584-fa273daa32a6',2,'Remove the chicken to a plate, then add the potatoes and chorizo to the pan. Continue cooking for 30 mins until the beans and potatoes are tender.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2f18bc78-b749-5be9-ba1e-76a328f01254','b4e9cab4-296d-5d77-8584-fa273daa32a6',3,'Discard the skin and bones from the chicken and tear into large chunks. Return the chicken to the pan with the spinach and simmer for 5 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('de1e4d79-186a-5036-8992-a5f2160d6ad0','ca3e822b-3bea-53cd-889e-cafc9429286f',1,'Boil the kettle. In a non-stick frying or shallow pan with a lid, fry the onion, peppers, chorizo and garlic in the oil over a high heat for 3 mins. Stir in the rice and chopped tomatoes with 500ml boiling water, cover, then cook over a high heat for 12 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4b1c5695-10ff-5ca4-a675-6d3f27706df0','ca3e822b-3bea-53cd-889e-cafc9429286f',2,'Uncover, then stir – the rice should be almost tender. Stir in the prawns, with a splash more water if the rice is looking dry, then cook for another min until the prawns are just pink and rice tender.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ee82e7b9-7c51-568f-8f9e-6a302c35fb3e','f30a891a-911c-5480-b495-322f4d921e9e',1,'Put the tomatoes in a bowl with the onion and thyme. Season, then drizzle with the vinegar and oil. Let the flavours mingle while you cook the chorizo.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a5f6aecd-4362-5d95-b6b7-ab88a53debe4','f30a891a-911c-5480-b495-322f4d921e9e',2,'In a hot, dry pan, fry the chorizo slices until browned on both sides. Serve the tomatoes with the fried chorizo, drizzled with a little oil from the pan.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d4e0090b-0dbc-5fb1-92b0-1316665603b9','12347e1f-4c39-5c5b-ad54-8321c6a74173',1,'Heat a large frying pan on a high heat and season the chicken. Add the olive oil to the pan, then the chicken. Brown for about 5 mins on each side, remove onto a plate, then set aside.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9db2e950-d9a0-52aa-b5e3-5e0e42dbde1c','12347e1f-4c39-5c5b-ad54-8321c6a74173',2,'Lower the heat to medium. In the remaining fat, fry the onions for 3 mins, then add the garlic and saffron. Cook for 3-4 mins more. Add the sherry, then simmer for 3-5 mins until syrupy.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
