('900518bb-f7e2-534b-868a-6a3d59f4767b','fabe75bd-d07c-5c49-96a3-3d3bc9e3e304',2,'Tip the raspberries into a pan over a medium-low heat along with the sugar and lemon juice. Cook for 5-6 mins until the berries have completely broken down. Push the mixture through a sieve set over a bowl, discarding the seeds. Stir in the gelatine leaves until dissolved (if they don’t dissolve, pour the mixture into a clean saucepan and heat gently until dissolved). Set aside to cool for 15 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e039c49a-364f-547c-aa31-0e1c2f1a5b04','fabe75bd-d07c-5c49-96a3-3d3bc9e3e304',3,'Whip the cream to soft peaks using an electric whisk, then gently fold this into the raspberry mixture. Spoon into the ramekins or moulds and chill overnight, or for at least 6 hrs. Serve with raspberries scattered over the top.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('1e679749-47c8-5513-b2a7-1463a061f51e','518ae6fc-ed78-577d-81fa-78d1edef1473',1,'Heat the oven to 180C/160C fan/gas 4. Melt 25g butter and generously brush into the holes of a mini bundt tins. Tip a little flour into each hole and shake to coat, then tip out the excess. Beat the butter, caster sugar and a pinch of salt together using an electric whisk. Add the eggs, one at a time, beating well after each addition. Combine the flour and baking powder in a separate bowl, then sift this into the wet ingredients and stir until smooth. Combine the cocoa powder and milk in a small bowl until smooth.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('811d90b2-261b-51a4-aa3e-6182d92c3a31','518ae6fc-ed78-577d-81fa-78d1edef1473',2,'Spoon 1 tbsp of the plain batter into each hole of the bundt tin. Mix the remaining plain batter with the cocoa powder mixture, then divide this between the holes. Bake for 15-18 mins, or until a skewer inserted into the cakes comes out clean. Leave to cool in the tin for 5 mins, then turn out onto a wire rack and leave to cool completely. Dust with icing sugar to serve.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c065358f-20ec-5882-9e45-e58b4d1b7ea5','518ae6fc-ed78-577d-81fa-78d1edef1473',3,'Pour 1 tablespoon of light batter into each mold. Mix the remaining batter with the stirred cocoa mixture and then fill the molds with a tablespoon.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('716f90d5-b8ee-5c98-9605-b0d2626e5c30','518ae6fc-ed78-577d-81fa-78d1edef1473',4,'Bake the mini Bundt cakes in the preheated oven for 15-18 minutes , depending on the size of the molds. After 15 minutes of baking time, use a toothpick to test with a skewer and, if necessary, bake for another 3 minutes. Let the mini Bundt cakes cool down completely in the tin. Then carefully remove from the mold. Dust with some icing sugar and serve. Enjoy your meal!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b316eb51-cb0e-5692-ab28-d294446ebcec','00879f8c-4433-5f3d-be57-be3806bef813',1,'Cut the meat into large pieces, put in your largest saucepan and cover with 5 litres water. Bring to the boil over a high heat, skimming away any foam that rises to the surface. Add the bay leaves. Season. Turn the heat down to a simmer and cook for 1 hr, or until the meat is soft and falls off the bone. Add the beans if using dried.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4fde28fa-1660-5e07-86b5-ad844b765cb8','00879f8c-4433-5f3d-be57-be3806bef813',2,'Turn the heat up. Bring back to the boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for another 20 mins – the beans should still be slightly raw. Add the carrots, onions, garlic and pepper. Stir well, then add the chillies, if using. Cook for 15 mins more.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d46843bc-26fe-586b-af28-8f39cfbeb35f','00879f8c-4433-5f3d-be57-be3806bef813',3,'Stir in the beetroot and cook for 10 mins before adding the potatoes. After 15 mins, add the tomato purée to taste and beans, if using canned, and bring to the boil. Cook for 5 mins, add the cabbage and cook for 5 mins more. Season, then garnish with the parsley and dill. Turn off the heat and leave to stand for 5 mins. Serve with soured cream on the side.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4077e006-040f-557e-b4f9-0a106b548784','a6b11dd8-c030-5603-9ff7-58f2d9f3b2e2',1,'Tip the flours, yeast and salt into a bowl. In a jug, mix the honey with 250ml warm water, pour the liquid into the bowl and mix to form a dough. Rye flour can be quite dry and absorbs lots of water, if the dough looks too dry add more warm water until you have a soft dough Tip out onto your work surface and knead for 10 mins until smooth. Rye contains less gluten than white flour so the dough will not feel as springy as a conventional white loaf.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('3073094f-fac6-567c-87ef-e6d7979dcabb','a6b11dd8-c030-5603-9ff7-58f2d9f3b2e2',2,'Place the dough in a well oiled bowl, cover with cling film and leave to rise in a warm place for 1-2 hrs, or until roughly doubled in size. Dust a 2lb/900g loaf tin with flour.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('63f0bf6f-cc5f-57c9-b0ed-d2035c536866','a6b11dd8-c030-5603-9ff7-58f2d9f3b2e2',3,'Tip the dough back onto your work surface and knead briefly to knock out any air bubbles. If using caraway seeds work these in to the dough. Shape into a smooth oval loaf and pop into your tin. Cover the tin with oiled cling film and leave to rise somewhere warm for a further 1 – 1.5 hr, or until doubled in size.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ea041d71-11cc-59a1-a28d-ba3836d29f94','a6b11dd8-c030-5603-9ff7-58f2d9f3b2e2',4,'Heat oven to 220C/200C fan/gas 7. Remove the cling film and dust the surface of the loaf with rye flour. Slash a few incisions on an angle then bake for 30 mins until dark brown and hollow sounding when tapped. Transfer to a wire cooling rack and leave to cool for at least 20 mins before serving',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4e061bb5-bac0-5e80-b720-d4c3b7c3af9e','ae2b0181-313f-5f21-99ea-3d13f46532d6',1,'Combine the yeast, a pinch of the sugar and a couple tablespoons of lukewarm water in a small bowl. Stir to dissolve the yeast, then leave for 10 mins until foamy.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c2a8893b-c5f4-5cab-a926-6bef7c21e4f0','ae2b0181-313f-5f21-99ea-3d13f46532d6',2,'Meanwhile, combine the flour, the remaining sugar and 2 tsp fine salt in a large bowl. Make a well in the centre, then add half the beaten egg, the yeast mixture and the oil. Pour in 200ml lukewarm water (it should feel slightly warm to the touch) and stir with a spoon, then mix using one hand, keeping the other clean while you bring the dough together. If there are a lot of very dry bits, gradually add a little water to just bring it together – you don''t want it to get too wet and sticky. The dough should be moist, but not soggy.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('639d9abe-8df5-560e-b4b4-cd2d385c3fb5','ae2b0181-313f-5f21-99ea-3d13f46532d6',3,'Once the dough has come together, turn it out onto a lightly floured surface. Knead using both hands for 10 mins until smooth and a bit springy. If it gets very sticky, add a very small amount of flour – as little as possible. A dough scraper is useful if the dough is sticking to the work surface. Stretch the sides of the dough down and pull together to form a ball. Lightly oil a bowl, then lightly roll the dough ball around the bowl so it''s coated in the oil. Cover with a clean tea towel and leave in a warm place for 1 hr, or until dough has doubled in size.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('af91f19e-228a-5ad6-9f0f-5fbd71c9e25c','ae2b0181-313f-5f21-99ea-3d13f46532d6',4,'Line a baking sheet with baking parchment. Turn the dough out onto a clean work surface and divide into three equal pieces, weighing for accuracy, if you like. Roll each piece into a long sausage shape about 25cm long, tapering them slightly at both ends. Lay the pieces out in front of you, parallel to one another with a couple centimetres between each. Bring the sausages together at the top end, then plait them down the length, tucking in the ends when you reach the bottom. Carefully transfer the loaf to the prepared baking sheet and loosely cover with a clean tea towel. Leave to rise until puffy and billowy, about 40 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f116bc18-5516-5b63-b917-8cd2d9bffb80','ae2b0181-313f-5f21-99ea-3d13f46532d6',5,'Meanwhile, heat the oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Gently brush the rest of the beaten egg all over the challah, getting it into all the crevices, and sprinkle with the poppy or sesame seeds, if using. Bake on a middle shelf of the oven for 25-30 mins, until the loaf is golden brown underneath and sounds hollow when tapped. Check after about 15 mins – if the top of the loaf has started to get too dark, cover it with foil. Leave to cool on a wire rack, then serve.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('adaf09bf-16d5-56a8-9af8-5c378c7576b3','3084a711-256b-5bc2-9428-1192238a15f4',1,'Whisk together mayonnaise, lemon zest and juice, vinegar, mustard and celery salt in a small bowl, then season generously.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f74d4374-2da5-5b17-9b0e-601afa8ad107','3084a711-256b-5bc2-9428-1192238a15f4',2,'Add cabbage, carrots, onion and celery. Mix well and refrigerate. Can be made up to 1 day ahead.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('52f5dec9-554e-5615-8e56-dbd7f0f862c8','2fb5887b-1b0c-592d-a1b3-cc4085c7e14e',1,'Heat the oven to 180C/160C fan/gas 4. Make the latkes by combining all of the ingredients.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b9416c23-d5b2-51dc-a03b-03ecd8a3abb4','2fb5887b-1b0c-592d-a1b3-cc4085c7e14e',2,'Heat the oil in a large non-stick pan. Spoon in the mixture to make six round latkes. Fry for 4-5 mins on each side, then transfer to a baking sheet and bake for 10 mins.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0d930297-17aa-54ed-83c0-50ca3e3b95c3','2fb5887b-1b0c-592d-a1b3-cc4085c7e14e',3,'Combine the yogurt and mint in a small bowl. Toss the salad leaves and tomatoes together, then serve the latkes with the mint yogurt and salad.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c29bcf22-00e2-5b4e-a50b-c98abb4a58e5','933a9f87-8a0a-5589-aeca-6010ad534ade',1,'Line the bottom of a springform of 20-2cm (8-9inches) with parchment paper, I usually leave some overhang as the batter is very liquid and may spill a bit. Preheat oven to 220 degrees Celsius.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e757f9eb-ad7c-51d5-bca5-3dee54db8567','933a9f87-8a0a-5589-aeca-6010ad534ade',2,'Grate the cheese and take out the ham.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('de380b1c-4c19-577e-9f64-1e3b485e0256','933a9f87-8a0a-5589-aeca-6010ad534ade',3,'Mix all remaining ingredients in a large bowl for about one to two minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ea9dd4d8-5569-5bda-a86f-20fdc438ecf2','933a9f87-8a0a-5589-aeca-6010ad534ade',4,'Pour half the batter into the prepared pan, it is going to be very liquid. Then place ham and cheese on top and pour the remaining batter on top.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e253eb0a-c47c-5030-85e9-6994edd510f5','933a9f87-8a0a-5589-aeca-6010ad534ade',5,'Bake for about 20-25 minutes or until top is golden. Wait for a few minutes before releasing from the pan and enjoy either hot or cold with some fresh herbs.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a465662f-c5ab-5fd8-aee3-c22987875f8b','ef0738cf-048d-52ed-8394-78f788ad24d4',1,'For the cookies cream the butter with the sugar for a few minutes. Then add the egg and honey and mix well. Add flour, cornstarch, cocoa, baking soda and baking powder and mix until you get a dough. Wrap in plastic wrap and chill for at least half an hour or overnight.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f5530341-4928-5f66-8700-6bde41a83be7','ef0738cf-048d-52ed-8394-78f788ad24d4',2,'Line two baking sheets with parchment paper, preheat oven to 200 degrees Celsius.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e7aff60e-27fb-5f52-a5d7-ab6230cbb259','ef0738cf-048d-52ed-8394-78f788ad24d4',3,'Divide dough into two parts, put one part back in the fridge before using. Roll out second part to about 2 millimeters and cut out round cookies with 5-6 centimeters in diameter. This can be done with a cookie cutter or glass. You should get 30 cookies in total or even more, I get about 40. Bake one baking sheet at the time for about 8-10min. Let cookies cool.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b551b85a-b9b6-57c4-9dd1-df779fec0c79','ef0738cf-048d-52ed-8394-78f788ad24d4',4,'For the filling look for two cookies of the same size and place about one teaspoon of dulce de leche onto the bottom one before sandwiching together.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('49365475-b826-5bc1-9507-a95e7e4a94f5','ef0738cf-048d-52ed-8394-78f788ad24d4',5,'Chop semi-sweet chocolate and melt with butter and orange zest on low heat. Dunk each sandwich cookie into the chocolate and let cool off on parchment paper before serving.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('366c3d1e-26e9-5b7b-85b5-4fc44587d2ec','cb1fd2c5-db3b-50ad-b4ba-beb6f1955ad7',1,'For the sandwich cookie cream the soft butter for about a minute, then add the sugar and cream for another two minutes. Incorporate the egg fully before mixing in the egg yolk. Once everything is nicely combined, add all remaining ingredients and mix one more time. Form dough into a ball and wrap in plastic wrap. Chill for at least half an hour or overnight.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('3246af27-0303-5462-8692-cf59dbe1611a','cb1fd2c5-db3b-50ad-b4ba-beb6f1955ad7',2,'Preheat oven to 180 degrees Celsius and line two baking sheets with parchment paper.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0ab39668-700a-5d0f-9fd0-23def307bb3d','cb1fd2c5-db3b-50ad-b4ba-beb6f1955ad7',3,'Divide dough in half, put one back in the fridge and roll out the other thickly on a lightly floured surface. Cut out cookies with either the bottom of a glass or a cookie cutter around 6cm in diameter. Repeat with all the dough.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('03012929-ecba-5f05-9e46-ccddf98159c1','cb1fd2c5-db3b-50ad-b4ba-beb6f1955ad7',4,'Bake for about 8-10min, the cookies will look very pale. Let cool off before filling half with each a teaspoon of dulce de leche. Place other half of cookies on top and roll the sides of each cookie in the coconut flakes (it helps if the dulce de leche was pressed down to the sides of the cookie). Enjoy.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('bd961395-e333-56b4-a38f-1c3ab975589e','b6441b05-956f-52e2-af97-d28d436a518f',1,'For the sponge cake preheat oven to 180 degrees Celsius and prepare either one or two 20cm/8 inch cake pan(s). Line bottom with parchment paper. Then divide the eggs into egg white and egg yolks. Use a bigger bowl for the egg yolks. If you have a glass or metal bowl, use that one for the egg whites. Be sure that bowl is free of fat/grease and that your mixer was properly cleaned. First beat the egg whites on medium speed with a pinch of salt until soft peaks form. Set aside. Without cleaning our mixer, beat the egg yolks with the sugar. Beat until the color becomes much paler and you have a creamy consistency. This usually takes several minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('36b0e776-f8a5-530b-b98d-505b52c7d99f','b6441b05-956f-52e2-af97-d28d436a518f',2,'Gently pour one third of the egg whites on top of the mixed egg yolks and sift the flour and cornstarch on top. Don''t skip this step. It is important that the flour mix was sifted. Gently mix all ingredients with a spatula. Try to incorperate the flour mix and egg whites without losing volume. Add the last two thirds of beaten egg whites and gently fold the mixture. Don''t overmix. Put batter into the prepared cake pans and immediately bake. Don''t let the batter sit for too long as it will quickly lose volume. Bake for 35 minutes if using one springform or 25 minutes if using two. Let cool a little before gently getting them out of the form. Tip: if making the day before, wrap in cling wrap, it is much easier to cut in half once cold.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c6849083-95e3-5648-8439-a90e94d0a673','b6441b05-956f-52e2-af97-d28d436a518f',3,'For the meringue beat egg white until soft peaks form, add pinch of salt and continue beating on high while adding the sugar. Beat for at least three more minutes until glossy and shiny. Pipe small stars or other shapes with the meringue on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper. Dry for about 45min at 100 degrees Celsius in the oven. Keep in airtight container until further use.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('594d7bb4-6358-50da-ac68-5617075420d4','b6441b05-956f-52e2-af97-d28d436a518f',4,'For the filling beat heavy cream, vanilla extract and sugar until stiff peaks form, slice peaches in thin slices. Cut cake in four layers, this is much easier done once the cake layers are cold. Brush cake layer with some of the peach juice left, then pipe thin layer of whipped cream around the edges, place the peach slices in the middle on first layer on cake, on the second layer only spread the dulce de leche. Repeat layer with brushed peach juice, whipped cream and peaches for the third and final layer. Be sure to reserve enough peach slices for the top. Spread thin layer of whipped cream on the sides of the cake and pipe on some roses around the edges if desired. Heat the peach juice and mix the cornstarch with a bit of water until you see no lumps. Once juice is hot, add the cornstarch and stir until glaze thickenes. Pour over peaches of the top layer cake. Crush the meringue and pat around the sides. Serve immediately.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8e0edc3b-2ded-55c8-93d7-f8b22cbaa6f0','01953337-ce15-501e-ab5f-c2790746a1c4',1,'For the filling place the can in a large pot and cover completely with water. Boil for two and a half hours, occassionally adding water. Let cool before opening. For further tips, please check here.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6283b52a-2141-56a5-b651-6e5ce02054fb','01953337-ce15-501e-ab5f-c2790746a1c4',2,'For the dough combine the flour, cocoa powder, and salt in a large bowl. Add the cold butter in small pieces and rub into crumbs with your fingers Add the egg and work into a dough. You may have to add milk, a tablespoon at a time if it still is to dry. Wrap and chill for at least half an hour or overnight.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f1048d13-9e09-57ae-94ae-b845e176d592','01953337-ce15-501e-ab5f-c2790746a1c4',3,'Line a baking sheeet with parchment paper and preheat the oven to 180 degrees Celsius.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('65d1d8c5-bdae-5f12-86dc-be0e36435200','01953337-ce15-501e-ab5f-c2790746a1c4',4,'Roll out the dough on a lightly floured surface, it should be thin. Cut out circles of 12cm either with a cookie cutter or with a smaller plate/dish. Put two to three teaspoons of the dulce de leche in the middle of each circle. Brush the edges with milk, I do this with my pinkie. Fold each circle in half so that you have a half moon and press down the edges with a fork. You can also turn the edges about half a centimeter inwards every centimeter or so to create a pattern.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6061c421-539d-5d4e-a8ab-ee16fb0dea4b','01953337-ce15-501e-ab5f-c2790746a1c4',5,'Place the prepared empanadas on the baking sheet and brush with egg wash. Bake for about 20-25min.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('66cc0425-a2af-56a3-8713-57c1000ceeb2','01953337-ce15-501e-ab5f-c2790746a1c4',6,'Towards the end of the baking time, melt the remaining butter and mix the sugar and cinnamon in a small bowl. Once you take the empanadas out, immediately brush with the butter and sprinkle with the sugar mix. Empanadas can be enjoyed either still warm or cold. If eating warm, be careful not to burn yourself with hot filling!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('cd80f003-78e7-590f-8db1-87415f254168','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',1,'Preheat oven to 410° F.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('df619798-44f9-50d7-aab0-a9c61c737510','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',2,'Pour the water into a large bowl. Make sure it is room temperature.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0c854f5b-7587-58d8-9d5f-bc369ab78fb8','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',3,'Add the salt. Blend well with a mixer, fork or spatula to make sure it dissolves well.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8c988974-5f50-5047-bfbe-dc771ebf2a1f','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',4,'While you continue to beat the mixture, slowly add the corn meal—a little bit at a time.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('511ee33c-e448-5176-888a-aa6e56b4233a','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',5,'Once all the flour is added, keep mixing until the corn meal, water and salt are thoroughly blended and dissolved.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4c03bf2a-4421-5b1b-a7bb-1b4fd203b2ec','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',6,'Set aside the masa in its bowl. Let it rest for 5 minutes so that the flour is thoroughly hydrated. This type of corn flour does not have any gluten, so it doesn’t need to be kneaded. The masa should be smooth, firm yet malleable.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('273cfe11-11b4-5f55-afca-a5a64b97edce','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',7,'While waiting for the 5 minutes’ rest, heat your budare (or comal, griddle, cast-iron pan or non-stick pan) over medium heat. Coat with a little bit of the oil.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e28c8fce-9c05-5259-9e96-2df2eaf9e2a7','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',8,'Fill a small bowl with water to wet your hands to make the arepas.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('810bdd50-f22c-5c99-8f54-0dfce1778a78','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',9,'Take about 2 Tbsp of the masa in your damp hands. The masa should fit easily in your palm so that it is easy to shape into a small ball.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7dc181d4-3c15-5cbf-a24d-cdfc7069a886','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',10,'Cross your hands, so that one is on top of the other, with the masa ball between them. Rotate your right hand in a circle, so that you are at the same time both pressing the masa into a flat disc and keeping its round shape.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('58ba2a38-c623-5ed6-842e-0bc0daf2b066','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',11,'arepa making',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('656254d4-14f5-5566-a314-e09de9339723','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',12,'The last step in shaping your arepa is to quickly pass and lightly press the masa disc from one hand to the other until it is about ¾ of an inch thick and 4 inches wide. Smooth the edges with your fingertips (quickly dip them into the water bowl first) so that they stay as round as possible and without cracks.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f6b4245f-0c1c-55a0-a8cf-1e8d43cfcbd3','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',13,'arepa making',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a3ce00a2-1a6b-5081-8c76-f641930e8230','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',14,'Place your arepas in batches on the preheated surface of your budare griddle or nonstick pan. Let each side turn golden, about 4 to 5 minutes per side. Check them often so that they don’t burn.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2b7bed08-7bfb-5f5c-a9c3-f95acf8e7005','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',15,'Once they are nicely browned on both sides, place the arepas on a baking sheet in your preheated oven for 10 minutes. They should be somewhat puffy, so that if you tap an arepa lightly on top, it will sound like you are tapping an empty box.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6c5c6c0e-db15-5321-acb7-abe7e71b0c8d','b8b2053f-50ad-5ccf-8c83-5450fe4b6ce9',16,'Serve arepas hot, whether you stuff with them with your choice of fillings or serve solo to accompany your favorite Venezuelan guiso or stew.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('daa6c52d-072f-5f23-a9c0-3c39da56c7ac','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',1,'Cook the meat: Place the flank steak in a pot with broth or water and salt. Cook over low heat for about 2 hours, until tender and easy to shred.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('cd972bb7-7f03-5b12-ad60-e24c17d18dd1','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',2,'Shred the meat: Once cooked, drain and shred the meat using two forks.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2ff59239-dcb9-5954-980b-8f0fc2502b89','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',3,'Prepare the vegetables: Sauté chopped onion, bell pepper, and garlic in a little oil. Add cumin, oregano, paprika, and salt. Stir in the meat and cook for a few minutes until the flavors are well combined.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c53602f1-84cb-50fe-951c-7947ab809274','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',4,'Make the dough: In a bowl, mix the cornmeal with warm water and salt until a soft dough forms. Let it rest for 5 minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ad4d552f-84ef-5a62-a469-4d3df679f771','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',5,'Form the arepas: Divide the dough into 6 portions, shape into balls, and flatten into thick discs.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d3ac8ecd-fd8a-52e4-9cd1-4e819f03e33a','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',6,'Cook: Cook the arepas on a griddle or skillet over medium heat for 2–3 minutes on each side until golden. You can then bake them for a few minutes if you prefer them crispier.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6760d0b3-fc29-5280-ab1f-44d2715cc8b6','49715ec7-1060-5ace-80be-c5dea84fd8db',7,'Fill: Slice the arepas open on one side, fill with the hot shredded beef, and top with grated cheese.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c23e050b-6136-58a2-9d5c-d3faf1795ca6','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',1,'The night before, break salt beef into big chunks and soak in water overnight, at least 8-10 hours. Put split peas into a bowl and cover with water to soak overnight.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0)
