('20f0cf3d-af2e-5ebe-9b11-5dc362726263','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',2,'Drain the salt beef and place it into a large stockpot. Cover with fresh water, at least 6-7 litres. Place the split peas into a pease pudding canvas bag or triple layer of cheesecloth and tie, making sure to leave room for peas to expand inside the bag.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('137afaf9-adf9-5db2-9080-8bce634f7e0e','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',3,'Put the bag inside the pot, tying the strings to the outside handle so it doesn''t stick to the bottom of the pot with the salt beef. Bring to a boil, then lower the heat and simmer for 2 hours.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('64cbe63a-952b-5f10-ad03-fb7b1aca2e7c','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',4,'Remove the peas pudding bag and empty contents into a bowl, mixing with butter and pepper for taste. Set aside.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('20c0b853-bd01-5748-a795-bbbe63c4f691','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',5,'Add your cabbage to the pot and boil for 20 more minutes. Then add turnip, carrots and potatoes then boil for 20 more, or until vegetables are tender.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('75d843d8-2ed2-56a0-83bb-b50313e351ab','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',6,'Remove salt beef and vegetables from the pot and put them on a platter.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9a6a3a99-181e-5982-a4af-0a3739f734cb','048341b9-139c-5fed-b34f-4fb6a668e64a',7,'Use the cooking liquid in two ways; as a pot liquor which some people like to drink or reduce it to make a jus or gravy to pour over the meal.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('532d7d03-a31e-5eb2-8599-5e37bfbb8595','1c3122dc-8306-590b-90f0-aaa48a1cca18',1,'Place the dried beans into a Dutch oven with 6 cups (1.5 L) of water. Soak overnight.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6aa4bd99-8d78-5723-8e57-6300f4749857','1c3122dc-8306-590b-90f0-aaa48a1cca18',2,'Drain and pour beans back into the pot with enough water to cover the beans by a couple of inches, cook for 30 minutes until they are tender but still firm. Drain beans, making sure to reserve cooking liquid, set aside.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e5589b7d-c318-56ee-839d-05226ca752cc','1c3122dc-8306-590b-90f0-aaa48a1cca18',3,'Preheat the oven to 325 °F (160 °C). While the oven is preheating, cook pork over medium-high heat in the Dutch Oven until fat is rendered and pork is beginning to brown, then add the onion cooking until tender.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7ec5a4fa-4499-57c7-8e10-8a85be336359','1c3122dc-8306-590b-90f0-aaa48a1cca18',4,'Add the beans back to the pot, along with molasses, brown sugar, apple cider vinegar, ground mustard, salt and pepper and 3 cups (750 mL) of reserved bean water.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8fd085c6-6764-5463-8d7b-3cd81a2e3c35','1c3122dc-8306-590b-90f0-aaa48a1cca18',5,'Bake uncovered for 3 to 5 hours until the beans are tender, and the sauce has thickened, and the edges of the pot get sticky.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f4640df6-36d1-5bb5-be89-6e84cc0d9875','1c3122dc-8306-590b-90f0-aaa48a1cca18',6,'(Note: if beans get dry, add another cup of water.)',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a363f1f5-3284-5f13-92eb-d5842f9ce8aa','553f6441-386b-51c5-8458-3513999c7ce9',1,'Preheat oven to 350°F (180°C). Grease an 8-inch (20 cm) square baking pan.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('bef55b4d-fc31-58a2-a446-9744f0af8e8a','553f6441-386b-51c5-8458-3513999c7ce9',2,'To make the date filing: Combine the dates and water in a medium saucepan over high heat and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to low and simmer gently, stirring occasionally until the mixture thickens, around 6 to 8 minutes. Remove from heat, stir in vanilla and let cool. Set aside.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a8f2c6aa-473b-55e7-8e37-4ef8851678c7','553f6441-386b-51c5-8458-3513999c7ce9',3,'Combine rolled oats, flour, sugar, baking soda and salt in a food processor. Pulse 3 times (careful not to overmix, you don’t want the mixture to be powdery, just combined). Add butter and pulse again until the mixture is crumbly in pea-sized clumps. Transfer to a mixing bowl to thoroughly mix in the butter.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8ae1b91a-eca4-50e6-aa39-c685351b266a','553f6441-386b-51c5-8458-3513999c7ce9',4,'Spread half of the oat mixture on the bottom of the prepared baking pan, pressing down to make a flat, equal bottom later. Add the date mixture over the crust and then spread evenly. Layer with the remaining oat mixture and press down to flatten the top layer.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('154624df-83c7-5ac3-9d49-bd2139539ab2','553f6441-386b-51c5-8458-3513999c7ce9',5,'Bake in the centre of the oven until the top is golden brown, 30 to 35 minutes. Let cool completely in the pan before cutting and serving. Date Squares keep well, covered in the refrigerator for up to a week, and frozen for 2 to 3 months.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0983503f-ec89-5f8e-8537-a1c3006a23e4','3d94cef0-3f2d-52a2-b30c-a3b7b75ef780',1,'Preheat the oven to 350 °F (180 °C) and line a large baking sheet with parchment paper.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('17e1a82d-5dce-5b48-921e-f2e4b9a7956c','3d94cef0-3f2d-52a2-b30c-a3b7b75ef780',2,'In a stand mixer with the paddle attachment, cream the butter, white sugar and egg until combined, then add the molasses and vanilla and mix until smooth.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('5fa330b1-2c25-55fe-b30c-2fb46bd26d8b','3d94cef0-3f2d-52a2-b30c-a3b7b75ef780',3,'Once combined, add the baking soda water mixture and mix for another minute to combine.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('240507c5-4929-5600-bd0d-380ef0ed8806','3d94cef0-3f2d-52a2-b30c-a3b7b75ef780',4,'Combine dry ingredients; mix baking powder, cinnamon, flour and salt in a separate bowl then add to the wet ingredients a little at a time, mixing on low until fully combined and scraping down the sides to ensure everything is incorporated. The dough should be easily shaped.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('287e8a4b-a28c-5cef-9bb0-3a2b467f9123','3d94cef0-3f2d-52a2-b30c-a3b7b75ef780',5,'Portion dough with a small spoon, roll them into balls and place them on the lined cookie sheet, press them into flat discs using a floured glass or your moistened palm.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
