('659e432c-5930-5945-aecd-cae9118df391','b4e6276e-09a6-50ea-8327-8dfc72db303f',7,'Drain the apples and potatoes and mash them together. Taste and add cinnamon and salt where needed. Remove the cinnamon stick before mashing',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ae7545cc-b0c3-5ad4-b63a-3d7db110eb9f','f1e898b8-4501-5594-8551-3d2766ecb062',1,'Place the flour in a large bowl and add the yeast and sugar. If the milk is cold make sure to heat it to lukewarm. Mix your flour mixture bit by bit with the milk until you have a smooth batter. Add the salt and mix with a wooden spoon till the batter is smooth and liquidy.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6faf161c-85ad-5290-ab32-83d78ef3a7cf','f1e898b8-4501-5594-8551-3d2766ecb062',2,'Cover with a clean tea towel and leave in a warm spot for about an hour to rise.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('1744a53e-066a-5d47-ae9e-de7e6b0f335b','f1e898b8-4501-5594-8551-3d2766ecb062',3,'Heat your deep fryer or add the oil to a large pot. The oil should be a t 180˚C (350˚F) for best results.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e5ece996-8123-551a-b768-3abc02165c91','f1e898b8-4501-5594-8551-3d2766ecb062',4,'Before starting stir your batter through and scoop the batter with two spoons or with an ice cream scoop. Let it drop into the oil carefully. It is easiest to do this if you dip your spoons or scoop into the oil before dipping into the batter. That way it will slide of the spoons easily. Don''t over crowd the fryer to prevent the oil cooling down too quickly and everything sticking together. Once one side is golden brown it usually turns around to the other side automatically. If not help it along with two forks.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7e0f9445-096e-5053-a815-47fab979cb44','f1e898b8-4501-5594-8551-3d2766ecb062',5,'Take the balls out once golden brown and leave to drain on a piece of kitchen paper.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('52b68b0d-cfd8-523f-a09e-201888965e20','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',1,'Place the dried yeast, milk and sugar in the bowl of your food processor. Mix and let stand for a few minutes until it begins to foam.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('787ec099-2a51-5e69-aef4-2cff06930faa','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',2,'Then add the flour, egg, butter, salt, 1 tsp of cinnamon and cardamom and process until smooth.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('edde132b-4ddf-5a05-ad2b-eed6fc2ea78a','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',3,'Form the dough into a ball, cover the bowl and let it rise for 1 hour or until it has doubled in size.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ce16cbb1-ef4c-5c61-a4bb-0f5eabc24501','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',4,'Mix the caster sugar with 1 tablespoon of cinnamon, pour over the dough and roll it in.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('44bebfcd-0bc5-5ae3-bda7-7431e33ee4c3','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',5,'Form 10 equal balls (about 75 grams each) and let them “sweat” for a while. The sugar will dissolve a little. When you roll them again later, the rest of the dough will absorb the sugar better.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e3969a91-b703-5ae4-ac68-430f639c6869','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',6,'Then roll the ball into a strand about 35-40 centimeters long while rolling through the powdered sugar.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7c789a69-46ef-5001-b673-2d60491e65f0','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',7,'Fold the strand around one end and tuck the other end under the bolus. Push something between the roll to secure the end.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c6f916b7-bec1-5210-bd22-2b8c14b22dd9','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',8,'Place on a baking sheet lined with a baking sheet, cover with plastic wrap and let them rise for ½-1 hour.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('205c9668-5cef-58c2-847b-f70111490c50','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',9,'Meanwhile, preheat the oven to 250 degrees Celsius/480 Fahrenheit top and bottom heat',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e63aa4c4-f445-54d7-bfeb-18aa4509895e','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',10,'Bake the Zeeland Boluses for about 8 minutes until done. Be careful – if you bake them too long, they will get dry and you will want something sticky 😉 .',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d48a1cf8-bc78-5791-83f4-1978697c1126','25a2e332-9b92-5a47-af88-fd1c15f1eb71',11,'Let them cool out of the oven for 1 minute, then turn them over and let them cool further (on a wire rack if necessary). Enjoy!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d7cd6d14-5914-5ab3-8860-a7ffeb8b3669','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',1,'Place flour in a bowl, and create a hole in the middle of the flour. Whisk eggs, and then pour whisked eggs into the well.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f01cbaae-e94d-5964-983b-c74e7dfc043a','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',2,'Add milk, and combine. Then, stir in the ground walnuts, baking powder and cardamom, and add to the mixture. Fold ingredients into the mixture until it forms an elastic dough consistency.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('88de1954-72b3-554a-998f-e19036fbcafb','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',3,'Take dough and with a rolling pin, roll out into a thin rectangle on a clean surface. Then, from the longest side of the rectangle, fold the dough into 3cm-wide lines, until the dough is fully rolled in a long line. Cut folded dough horizontally into 3cm pieces',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('30fe3c49-b9ab-5b63-90ef-478a98da054c','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',4,'Heat a deep pan of the vegetable oil, and wait till it reaches frying temperature. Whilst you are waiting. Fill a deep pan with 1 litre of water, and bring to the boil.  Then, pour in the sugar, and stir gently until it becomes thick and syrup-like. Turn down the heat and leave to simmer.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('de4dc429-2c35-5c79-98fb-780dbf2be06a','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',5,'Carefully lower each piece of dough into the frying oil. Fry until golden brown.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('770b3e61-b1f8-55c3-83b6-55732eaae669','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',6,'When golden brown, take the Baghlaw pieces out of the oil, and place them into the sugar syrup to coat.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0d49e96e-1049-54d8-96e2-7c5fd93d5aac','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',7,'Remove from the syrup and whilst still warm, sprinkle with ground walnuts, so they stick to the Baghlaw.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a4241643-731f-5096-bf97-19cb7ba34e49','918cca36-9920-5392-b46b-bc9e399cb294',8,'Leave to cool. Then, enjoy with your friends and family!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('751fb1c1-d4a7-5786-b2b5-98dd354fb852','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',1,'Place the meat cut into pieces, in a large pan with the onions. Add the turmeric and enough water to cover. Bring to the boil then cook gently until the meat is very tender and can easily be removed from the bones.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f9494fd8-13a9-577b-a7b5-998dd57380e6','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',2,'While the meat is cooking, cut the orange peel into thin match style pieces, removing as much pith as possible. Leave to soak in a bowl of water.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('82e4f863-524d-5870-bc3b-b2e8221f228a','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',3,'When the meat is tender, remove from the pan and when cool enough, remove the meat from the bones and shred the meat into strips with your hands. Return the meat to the pan.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9b8680a9-6e17-5fa3-8e1b-f9fea7327703','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',4,'Wash the short grain rice and then add to the pan with salt according to taste. The juices should cover the rice by about 2cm, add more water if necessary. Bring back to the boil, then reduce the heat to medium and cook with the lid off, stirring from time to time until the rice is "al dente" and the liquid is absorbed.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8cdfa831-ab80-598c-906a-c6ef2645c3c2','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',5,'Add the natural yoghurt, and stir in well but carefully. Fry the crushed cloves of garlic in the oil and add to the dish along with the dill, black pepper, the chickpeas and extra salt to taste.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('99df4d42-d31e-5a85-8da1-a9851d2d0d09','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',6,'Mix in well, then cover the top of the pan with a clean thick cloth and the lid. Leave on a low heat for about half an hour to allow the flavours to absorb.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0587025b-e476-5196-a61f-6477b166db85','13b50eb7-08a8-535a-8e3e-07e2522353c0',7,'Enjoy with some warm nan bread for extra comfort.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9b0ea7c5-5709-59c5-9a69-4878b396d974','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',1,'To prepare the dough, sift the flour with 1tsp of salt into a mixing bowl. Slowly mix in as much of the water is required, until a stiff dough is formed. Knead on a clean work surface for 5-10 minutes, until the dough is elastic and shiny. Cover with a damp cloth and set aside for about an hour.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('74532eb6-e039-5079-97b6-558139e85ddd','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',2,'Put the chopped lamb, onions, chilli, 1 tsp salt, ground pepper and spices in a bowl and mix thoroughly.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('39b3603e-062c-52fe-8b4c-8951e17faac3','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',3,'Divide the dough into 4 small balls, and roll out to a thickness of 1.5mm, cutting into 10cm squares. Into each square, place 1 heaped teaspoon of the lamb mixture.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('79c68861-13f4-5cd3-88b5-22d54fcc59bf','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',4,'Take two opposite corners and bring them to join in the centre by nipping together firmly between your fingers, and then bring together to other two corners in the same manner. Note that the mantu should not be entirely closed, as the steam has to be penetrate and cook the filling!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('4b21ab06-680a-5171-9f37-b1833a3539ae','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',5,'Using fat to grease the shelves of the steamer, place your mantu so that there is a small space between each one. Steam for 30-45 minutes over a medium heat.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('58f4d6ed-e57b-5276-8759-b1eed3c01dea','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',6,'Meanwhile, make the tomato sauce. Heat the oil in a pan, add tomato puree, and bring to the boil. Stir and simmer on a low heat until the mantu are ready.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('809afcea-8539-5136-b7f1-6c8dca5e6998','e0fdd0aa-0cc2-5e6d-9e13-357aa1aa7baa',7,'Remove the mantu carefully from the steamer and place on a large, warm dish. Spoon the tomato sauce over the top, followed by the strained yoghurt, and sprinkle with chopped coriander to garnish.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a351e04a-ca0e-586d-9155-bcbb55c2ce9a','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',1,'Remove the skin of the pumpkin. Also remove the inner seeds.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('171a06f5-2ea0-54ad-af6c-2f4a484406d4','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',2,'Cut the flesh into 2cm cubes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('fa3e38a6-214d-548c-896c-d24ee2215801','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',3,'Take the zest off the oranges, with as little pith as possible, and cut into matchstick-sized strips.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9f01e82c-fa82-5574-9762-651da52866ef','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',4,'Extract the juice from the oranges. Remove the seeds from the cardamom pods and reserve.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2aa39d92-0ab9-52a9-970c-1f85b3b2d20c','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',5,'Place the pumpkin, orange juice, orange strips, sugar and whole cardamom pod seeds in a large pan, mix well and leave to marinate for about 10 hours or overnight. Stir occasionally.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c363f04c-1857-5f6d-a88a-6bb44003153c','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',6,'Bring the mixture to the boil, then reduce the heat and simmer until the liquid has thickened and become syrupy. This can take about an hour or a little bit longer.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('fcb22f00-245e-5563-939c-ac025bb11fe5','805d91db-6819-5a98-a1b0-f993d2975d70',7,'Leave to cool then place in clean, dry jars. Enjoy!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9e402f42-b59e-5d79-96bb-fc365e7e7cff','8a7dd2ae-be85-574e-98e9-690d7b92e9e1',1,'Baking the Lamb',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8b093406-7a2e-5582-9ce5-95dddc7a6179','8a7dd2ae-be85-574e-98e9-690d7b92e9e1',2,'In a large pan (with a lid) melt the butter and olive oil together then add the diced lamb. Brown the lamb on a medium heat, this will take around 5 minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b17b5cd7-bddd-5203-b110-b609f7f83d75','8a7dd2ae-be85-574e-98e9-690d7b92e9e1',3,'Add the garlic, oregano, 300ml of water and season with salt and pepper. Mix well before covering with the lid. Leave to simmer for 50 minutes mixing a couple of times ensuring the lamb doesn’t start to burn.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('30cd86f2-2940-5616-a15c-1d88033b6276','8a7dd2ae-be85-574e-98e9-690d7b92e9e1',4,'The juices should have nearly all boiled away so another 150ml of water should be added along with the rice. Mix altogether, bring to the boil, place the lid on and leave for just 10 minutes. It’s advised to check at around 8 minutes – you want the liquid to be evaporated with just moist coating of oily water left over the lamb and rice.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f5e954f6-31c0-5163-8b3b-35aa5b088125','8a7dd2ae-be85-574e-98e9-690d7b92e9e1',5,'Place the lamb and rice into a casserole dish, the mixture should fully cover the base and have at least 2 inches spare for the yogurt. Alternatively you can split into four ceramic bowls.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
