('61110de3-5654-5af1-a2fc-891e66fd0ce4','d1eb4542-aaf9-5805-82ce-8fd3d72822b2',1,'Put the corn flour in a bowl and add the salted water little by little, mixing with the flour until all the water has been used and the flour has become a dough. Let it rest for five minutes. Now, shape the dough into round rolls about 3 inches in diameter and 1/2 inch thick. In a lightly greased skillet, slowly cook the arepas until a crust forms on each side. Now place them into a casserole and bake in the oven at 350 degrees for approximately 20 minutes, until the arepas sound hollow when tapped.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('17a4b182-9d96-5f97-9712-84e43feb1c7f','d1eb4542-aaf9-5805-82ce-8fd3d72822b2',2,'To enhance taste: instead of using just water, use chicken or beef broth.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e9d6b3be-7289-52af-aa3a-d159733c9751','edeff498-ae7e-5fe3-96ae-418985e02db8',1,'Peal the bananas and boil them together with the cinnamon, vanilla extract, sugar and water for about 20 minutes. Bake the bananas in the oven at 275°F for 10 minutes. Serve with favorite ice cream.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6a701241-fea0-5a6d-94ca-f1a53deeb805','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',1,'First boil the rice for eight minutes. Meanwhile, peel and finely chop the onion. Then chop the herbs.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d8e54dbe-1d5a-59cf-9d13-fc0420add098','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',2,'The recipe didn''t really say what to do with the chickpeas (also known of course as garbanzo beans), beyond soaking them overnight and rinsing them. I used canned chickpeas, since I''ve never actually seen them dried. I decided to chop/mash them slightly so they would better incorporate into the filling.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('988621fb-dbfc-5ed4-9cc2-a031a858fd62','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',3,'Chickpeas (or garbanzo beans) roughly chopped',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('aebe6946-1316-5c8f-b07d-d789a3466f10','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',4,'Now mince the lamb (I used my mini food processor). Here''s where I ran into another problem: what to do with the lamb fat this recipe calls for? Mince it? Melt it? Does lamb fat even melt? I decided to mince mine. Thankfully, my husband doesn''t actually read this blog because he''d be horrified if he knew I put fat in the dolma on purpose.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ff8ffc2e-5a6e-5514-8a66-2c9c4dee418a','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',5,'Minced lamb and its good friend, minced fat. Ew.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a70c7532-968c-521b-a595-25bb01c8c9bd','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',6,'The ingredients for the dolma stuffing include onion, cilantro, chickpeas and turmeric.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('d2997193-ee24-53ff-88fb-8e836003d04d','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',7,'Anyway, now get your hands into all that slimy raw meat and mix in the onion, spices, chickpeas, rice, chopped herbs and fat. Add a little salt and pepper for good measure. In fact, based on my results I would say to err on the side of a little extra salt and pepper.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('740d4623-4fae-5cb7-a5c0-dc566afb3bd9','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',8,'Mix well with your hands until the stuffing looks something like this.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('677e0c26-e252-5088-a152-c1427bb2579c','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',9,'Fill the biggest saucepan you own with salted water and bring it to a boil over high heat. Now pull the outer leaves off of the cabbage (save them) and drop the rest of it, whole, into the water. Let it boil for three or four minutes, turning it if the water level isn''t quite high enough to completely cover it.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c468bec1-d5de-5a45-9bc5-3e44206aac06','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',10,'The reason you are doing this is because it''s difficult to get whole cabbage leaves off of an American cabbage. The cabbages you typically buy in our supermarkets come in very tight round balls, and because the leaves are crispy they will snap and crack when you try to pull them off in an un-blanched state. Blanching them for a few minutes makes it so they will come right off without tearing.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('aa747db0-f1ca-5798-9950-e4314018a6e2','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',11,'Now carefully take the cabbage out of the water (but keep the water boiling) and let it cool for a minute or two so you don''t burn your fingers. Carefully pull the leaves off the cabbage, cutting them at the base if you have to do so to loosen them. Try to get them off in one piece. If the inner leaves are still crispy, return the cabbage to the boiling water for another three or four minutes. Repeat until all of the useable leaves are free.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('360cf08b-f1e2-5b23-8023-0fa25d8732ea','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',12,'Blanched cabbage leaves',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('357952f5-73c0-501c-84d2-f3ca427dbb05','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',13,'Now put the leaves on a cutting board and cut out the tough stalks (save them). Cut the largest leaves in half.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b7d88283-366f-5487-a006-5263cc7df7d8','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',14,'Remove the tough inner stalk and set aside. Cut larger leaves in two.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('6caf11a1-f129-5e9b-b381-4b13796b7d51','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',15,'Put a heaping tablespoon of the filling in the middle of each leaf, making a short cylinder shape. Fold the ends over the filling, then roll tightly (as if you are making a tiny burrito).',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b78f8910-0405-55c7-8b13-1bc1d05e6967','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',16,'This is not much of a cylinder, but you get the idea.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('db58f40e-8f04-589c-8503-872d69844b2e','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',17,'Fold the edges over ...',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('3cdd166e-6b85-5481-8709-2889aa079ea9','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',18,'Then roll, as if you were making a really small burrito.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2d0428dc-764e-5825-9671-c190de53bd12','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',19,'Your finished dolma should look kind of like this, only without the hole in the middle.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('cfb7300e-7b59-50d9-854e-3a50fd46854c','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',20,'Put all of the discarded cabbage leaves, stalks etc. into the bottom of a stockpot. I know, this seems a little strange. What you''re basically going to be doing is steaming the dolma, with the discarded cabbage pieces forming the base of your steamer. Carefully place the dolma on the bed of cabbage leaves.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('1d0c81dd-006d-55df-9742-f82eb9cabad5','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',21,'These dolma are resting on top of discarded cabbage leaves.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b6750769-bc6a-5cc6-894a-7300628bbbb1','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',22,'Add water to the stockpot up to about the top of the discarded leaves. Don''t cover the dolma.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('5b184ca6-2f17-57fa-8e7c-faa6af87cbff','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',23,'Now here''s where you have to get a bit creative. The dolma needs to be weighted down so it doesn''t unwrap during cooking. I used a metal pie pan, and then I put my mortar on top of it. You could also use a dessert plate with something heavy on top of it, but it would need to be an oven-safe one.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7526d6ef-0415-595a-a192-3641eac19224','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',24,'The dolma need to be weighted down during cooking so they don''t unwrap. Just improvise.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a46eea33-e6c4-58dc-a579-b508ddb1c0b9','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',25,'Bring the water to a boil, then simmer for 25 minutes.You might have to use your ears to figure out if the water is actually boiling; I personally couldn''t see what was in my pot after I weighted it down.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e78e6eee-c715-5ef1-8ebd-2432331bde89','bb684f2d-3b0f-5983-b3c8-371e63fe2b0c',26,'Meanwhile, make a simple tomato sauce out of the tomato paste and water. Heat it up for a few minutes over a medium flame. After the dolma have been cooking for 25 minutes, pour the sauce over them and cook for another five minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8396cc9b-466b-58a4-8e25-95f484b01ef4','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',1,'If you are using rohu fish it will usually be frozen. Soak it in cold water for 30-45 minutes to defrost and while still a little firm, descale and cut each steak into quarters and wash in cold saltwater a few times. Drain and set aside. If using an alternative such as cod, cut into 2 ½ inch chunks then rinse, drain and set aside',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('5b3b3e9c-7ad6-5dc6-a257-d1b061a4de1f','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',2,'Top and tail the daikon and peel using a potato peeler. Cut in half widthways then cut each half down the middle, lengthways. Now slice into 2cm-thick half-moon pieces. Rinse and set aside',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8a13e003-8c7f-57e6-bca6-421ce61514db','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',3,'Place a large, shallow saucepan over a medium heat and add the oil. When the oil is hot add the crushed garlic and stir for a minute until pale golden',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('dd8d50c9-7910-57ee-b40e-9803bed67354','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',4,'Add the onion paste and salt and cook for 3-5 minutes, until the onion softens and becomes translucent, stirring occasionally',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2c752b38-8a08-52b5-b219-c1656bb4113f','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',5,'Pour in 200ml of water then cover and cook for 10 minutes, stirring once or twice',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('27a6cd1a-f895-5339-9b58-b9f8910d53a4','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',6,'After 10 minutes add the ground spices and stir for a couple of minutes so that the spices cook through. Cover and cook for 5 minutes over a low heat then stir in the daikon. After a minute or so add 200ml of water. Cover and cook for 10 minutes on a medium heat',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('93d2ab3c-e092-5570-8e09-64e89f6b9d4b','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',7,'Add the fish pieces to the pan and mix thoroughly so that the fish is coated in the spices. Gently shake the pan and cover and cook for 5 minutes on medium heat. It is very important not to stir the pot after this stage',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0427afeb-4f7b-515b-9005-3ac6d7013320','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',8,'Meanwhile, boil some water. After the 5 minutes are over carefully pour 500ml hot water into the pan. When doing this pour into the sides of the pan so that you don’t pour boiling water directly onto the fish',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('31ba2cff-b184-59e1-99b6-544f31c65d36','2bf11e04-4511-5fb9-9880-e870b892b33a',9,'Give the pan a gentle shake then cover and simmer over high heat for 15 minutes. Add the chopped coriander and chillies and continue cooking for another 5 minutes then turn off the heat. Serve immediately with rice and the lime wedges',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('17467aeb-c8d2-503b-b154-c51193060233','8a93e15a-f0e9-5ceb-a47b-8668fe6c8516',1,'Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook and stir the onions in the hot oil until translucent, about 5 minutes. Add the ginger-garlic paste and continue cooking another 5 minutes. Reduce heat to medium; stir the tomatoes into the mixture and cook until the tomatoes are pulpy, 5 to 10 minutes. Season with the cayenne pepper, curry powder, garam masala, turmeric, and cumin; cook and stir another 5 minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('565b2425-d9d6-5532-a9d6-76bba1f80112','8a93e15a-f0e9-5ceb-a47b-8668fe6c8516',2,'Add the chicken and potatoes to the mixture in the skillet; simmer, stirring occasionally, until the potatoes are tender and the chicken is no longer pink in the center, about 20 minutes. Sprinkle the cilantro over the mixture and continue simmering another 10 minutes. Serve hot.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a41a9ce7-7fe7-5be9-9afd-e1ece544a284','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',1,'In a large bowl, combine the butter and caster sugar until creamy. Add the egg and a pinch of salt.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('956aa4b9-693b-568a-8535-f8985aa39c45','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',2,'Stir into a buttery mixture. Add the sifted flour.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2601d07d-4ec4-5e94-b344-5e34b044ad59','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',3,'Whisk well. You should end up with a smooth dough. Cover it with a piece of plastic wrap and put the dough in the fridge for 15 minutes to chill and set.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c028e6ba-397f-5753-922a-6cfd46259a5b','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',4,'In the meantime combine the cassonade (or brown sugar) and the cinnamon.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('edb96550-faf4-5e47-96e3-809565ee1cf1','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',5,'Transfer the dough onto a floured surface and knead it for a minute. Add extra flour if necessary. Roll the dough out gently into a nice rectangle. It should be about ⅕-inch (5 mm) thick. Sprinkle with the sugary cinnamon mixture.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('0d3e75df-f93d-5c78-affc-1e39abb46f35','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',6,'Carefully start rolling the dough up. If it is too sticky, put it in the fridge again for a couple of minutes. Wrap it up tightly in plastic wrap.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8a4bd19d-185e-54c2-bfbd-be227a53770a','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',7,'Put it in the fridge for 30 minutes to chill and set. After that, remove the cling film and cut the dough roll into even slices.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('1df986c9-d729-5a46-98a4-4260cf004d13','fe6a43aa-fd9c-5be7-bb1f-2ae59e8997a9',8,'Place the slices on a baking paper lined baking tray. Bake the cookies in a preheated oven at 356°F (180°C) for 14 to 16 minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
