('9424e0c9-e839-50ab-8b66-815a6a6c1d72','52cb6ae1-7c2e-5779-bbff-950ffa18b4d7',1,'Peel and chop the onion and garlic. Add both to a large pan with the butter and place it over medium heat.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('c971f532-8062-5419-902c-7686d9acf98a','52cb6ae1-7c2e-5779-bbff-950ffa18b4d7',2,'Let the onion and garlic sweat for 5 minutes. Then add the chopped potatoes, bay leaves and thyme and stir well. Cook for another 5 minutes.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7327338e-0b5a-5905-9658-af572aee4e83','52cb6ae1-7c2e-5779-bbff-950ffa18b4d7',3,'In the meantime peel and slice the carrots. Peel the turnip. Dice it into bite-size pieces. Slice the leek in half lengthwise. Rinse it well to remove any sand. Add the vegetables to the potatoes and onion. Also add the mustard and chicken stock and season with pepper and salt.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('cae34b5f-6240-5a60-a9a5-6ef3df770405','52cb6ae1-7c2e-5779-bbff-950ffa18b4d7',4,'Stir all the ingredients well and cover the pan with a lid. Cook the hutsepot for about 20 to 25 minutes or until all the vegetables and potatoes are tender. Stir regularly. Add extra water if necessary. In the meantime pan fry the sausages in a little oil or butter until golden brown and cooked through. Keep warm.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('20e74233-1815-543c-90f8-9bfdee032608','52cb6ae1-7c2e-5779-bbff-950ffa18b4d7',5,'Once the potatoes start to fall apart, stir and turn it all into a mushy and chunky vegetable stew. Check the seasoning and add extra pepper, salt or mustard to taste.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('1ecc5b28-0b57-57d0-8ca4-6d59aa20f732','52cb6ae1-7c2e-5779-bbff-950ffa18b4d7',6,'Scoop the hutsepot onto deep plates and top with the sausage. Serve hot with an extra dollop of mustard if you like.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b90c6a3c-0faf-5129-aa5e-1c8a801bc989','b8b7779a-74bf-539e-aea6-915dcdbb9bdc',1,'Let the frog legs soak in the milk in the fridge for an hour (optional).',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8f64e96f-e453-5e4a-8b62-dc437582d282','b8b7779a-74bf-539e-aea6-915dcdbb9bdc',2,'Rinse the legs and pat them dry with kitchen paper.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e675214a-1c5f-5d15-b4fc-8971d770ac7e','b8b7779a-74bf-539e-aea6-915dcdbb9bdc',3,'Add the olive oil and half of the garlic butter to a large wok or frying pan. Place it over high heat until the butter starts to foam. Don''t let it burn.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('84ab4c43-a89c-551a-9c10-8be26cdda1d6','b8b7779a-74bf-539e-aea6-915dcdbb9bdc',4,'Add the frog legs to the pan. Pan fry them for about 10 minutes until they are golden brown on both sides. Turn the over regularly.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('fbf73143-56de-5878-b3cb-6725a66d242b','b8b7779a-74bf-539e-aea6-915dcdbb9bdc',5,'Add the rest of the garlic butter right in the end together with the freshly chopped parsley. Season with a pinch of pepper and salt to taste.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a9d74f02-241d-54c1-a7bf-a2120b67a7af','b8b7779a-74bf-539e-aea6-915dcdbb9bdc',6,'Divide the frog legs over plates. Serve with grilled bread and a green salad.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8cedf5fd-6c53-56ef-b3fe-b90f8c765a40','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',1,'Put the chicken, water and one garlic clove in a large saucepan. Place it over medium-high heat until boiling. Then turn the heat low, cover the pan and simmer the chicken for 10 minutes. Remove the chicken leg and breast. Keep the fresh chicken stock for later.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9b8988d6-68af-524b-9458-1ae4be135e57','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',2,'Let the chicken cool. Then dice the chicken breast up. Pick the meat off the leg. Discard any bones and skin. Slice the leek, celery and carrot finely (julienne). Add the butter, rosemary and bay leaves to a large pan and place it over medium heat until melted.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('82dd880f-29c3-504a-bc01-a95a960755db','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',3,'Then add the sliced vegetables. Season with pepper and salt.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('5983c179-5e63-5c08-adc9-5dd9bafe94cd','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',4,'Stir and cook the vegetables for 3 minutes. Then add the shredded and diced chicken.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f6b74b22-0c22-551f-b6ba-d1f9816d8dcf','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',5,'Cover the pan and cook the chicken and vegetables for 5 minutes. Then add the cream and ½ cup (120 ml) of the fresh chicken stock.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('bcc1af29-67f8-5cbc-9823-f9f998392280','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',6,'Look at this delicious waterzooi recipe! Do try out my chunky chicken stew with fresh leeks, celery, carrots and lots of cream... This is Belgian comfort food!',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('a08751ab-1726-55a8-a5e7-0cd36d137003','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',7,'Cover the pan and cook the stew for 20 minutes until the potatoes are tender. Add the egg yolk and 2 tablespoons of the warm cream from the pan to a cup. Whisk and add it back to the pan to thicken the sauce.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('9dbf1f69-9445-5dfe-9f16-134b474bcf9f','c37a8b6f-86dc-5cc1-a372-85a3544f286e',8,'Stir all the ingredients and then turn the heat very low. Check the seasoning and add extra pepper or salt to taste. Remove the rosemary and bay leaves. Divide the stew over deep plates and drizzle with the remaining cream sauce. Serve hot.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('21a7219b-6a82-5483-8e6e-9071658e1591','a38005cb-0448-553b-8c9a-83ff235f4b59',1,'Scrub the potatoes well but don''t peel them. Cut them into bite-size pieces. Add them to a large pan water and a pinch of salt. Bring it to a good boil. Cook the potatoes until tender and then remove them using a slotted spoon. Keep the potatoes at room temperature.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('7bcee671-0bf8-5ebe-82e6-f58e4d8764f0','a38005cb-0448-553b-8c9a-83ff235f4b59',2,'Trim and clean the green beans. Add them to the pan of hot water you boiled the potatoes in. Cook the green beans until nearly tender (keep them crunchy). Strain and refresh them immediately under cold running tap water to stop the cooking process.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('95999c91-7bc5-566f-8498-4c6e967d0cf7','a38005cb-0448-553b-8c9a-83ff235f4b59',3,'Add the bacon to a large non-stick pan and place it over medium heat. Cook the bacon for a couple of minutes until cooked through. Then take the pan off the heat and let the bacon cool down a little.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0)
