('2fccc29b-ce69-50ec-912e-7f0a875b9d24','a38005cb-0448-553b-8c9a-83ff235f4b59',4,'Combine the olive oil, vinegar and mustard. Transfer the cooked potatoes, green beans, bacon, chopped onion, parsley and vinaigrette. Season with pepper and salt.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('117aed68-f7a4-5c61-a058-9451009acb90','a38005cb-0448-553b-8c9a-83ff235f4b59',5,'Stir well. Check the seasoning and add extra vinegar, pepper or salt to taste. Transfer the salad to a large serving bowl or 2 deep plates and garnish with the boiled eggs. Serve lukewarm.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('dd5c65d3-87f2-5b41-9591-1f7ef3d8db2e','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',1,'Add the chopped potatoes and garlic to a high pan and fill it with tap water until the potatoes are fully submerged.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('fe27f6ea-2f4e-5ab0-88c0-6d75562a2fa0','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',2,'Add some salt. Then place the pan over high heat and bring the potatoes to a boil. Cook them until tender. In the meantime rinse and drain the savoy cabbage. Slice it up finely.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('2f261dd7-817c-5d2e-a201-eb81dfe23697','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',3,'Add a tablespoon of butter to a large non-stick pan. Place it over medium-high heat. Once melted, add the savoy cabbage. Season with a pinch of pepper and salt.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('de78a34d-bc66-5d37-b63f-5d4a65642910','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',4,'Stir fry the cabbage for 15 to 20 minutes or until the cabbage is soft and tender. Then turn the heat off and take the cabbage off the heat. In the meantime, pan fry the sausages (or sliced bacon if you are using both) in a non-stick pan in a tablespoon of butter or oil until golden brown and cooked through.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('25a2cda8-6976-5393-a2d5-8909a69175bd','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',5,'Transfer the sausages (and bacon) to a plate and cover with a lid or tinfoil to keep the meat warm. In the same greasy pan, add the sliced onion and extra butter and cook it gently over medium heat for 10 minutes until softened. (I often add diced bacon as well, if I only serve the stoemp with sausages.)',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('ff0d3ff0-1621-58b9-942d-7deb4eaabdf1','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',6,'Then add the beer and turn the heat up. Let the beer reduce until you get a nice beer and onion sauce (you can add a little flour or sauce thickener if you like). Add the pan fried meat back to the pan and cover to keep warm.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('8b602563-3f8c-52cf-844f-963d9cbc3fd8','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',7,'Drain the cooked potatoes and garlic, add them back to the pan you cooked them in together with the pan fried cabbage and chopped parsley. Sprinkle with some pepper, salt and nutmeg. Also add the milk and the rest of the unsalted butter.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('b8fcadcd-6e43-5451-9762-c762f380bc98','e2a779d5-c1d4-59f8-9730-46e04ef80bf1',8,'Mash the potatoes, parsley and cabbage up. Add extra butter or milk if necessary. Also check the seasoning and add extra pepper, nutmeg or salt to taste if necessary. Scoop the cabbage mash onto plates and top with the pan fried sausages (and bacon). Drizzle with the beer and onion sauce. Serve hot.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('20bf25ab-f70e-5efe-aefe-29885f84692b','b2d53db9-1ca4-5989-b38c-89a0914e81d7',1,'Cut the beef into 1-inch chunks. Dredge the beef in the flour until all of the beef sides are covered.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('f43b0b22-aeb3-5e12-9aef-9a89d23c830e','b2d53db9-1ca4-5989-b38c-89a0914e81d7',2,'In a large soup pot, melt the butter over medium high-heat. In small quantities, brown the beef on all sides, removing the browned beef and setting it aside in a large bowl as you go. When the beef is browned, add the onion and the garlic to the pot. Sauté the onion and garlic for one minute, scraping the bottom of the pot as you stir.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('abfc7559-5a9b-57c5-aa54-b2cf05c8bfa7','b2d53db9-1ca4-5989-b38c-89a0914e81d7',3,'Return the browned beef to the pot and add the beef stock, pumpkin puree, Worcestershire sauce, salt, and pepper. Stir well and bring to a boil. Once the liquid is boiling, reduce heat to medium-low and simmer for 3 hours, stirring occasionally.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('04642d5c-d95e-566b-bf63-380344c3edee','b2d53db9-1ca4-5989-b38c-89a0914e81d7',4,'Add the potatoes, carrots and thyme sprigs to the pot and increase heat to medium. Cook for an additional 30 minutes. Salt to taste and serve.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e915d1fc-20f9-541b-986f-f1f419392806','d1dac293-8467-53df-b455-3c3469bf23cd',1,'Pre heat the oven to 160 degrees Celsius. Cut the meat into large chunks then brown in a dish suitable for slow cooking in the oven such as a cast iron casserole dish.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('e0d1fd67-dd94-5a96-8272-33b22e907be4','d1dac293-8467-53df-b455-3c3469bf23cd',2,'Add the whole peeled onion, salt, cracked black pepper, water and bay leaves. Bring to the boil then cover and place into the oven for 4 hours.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('76d0a6ca-2e8f-5855-855c-1023d97da1be','d1dac293-8467-53df-b455-3c3469bf23cd',3,'After 4 hours, remove from oven and place onto the stove burner in order to cook off most of the remaining liquid. Use a wooden spoon to pound or mash up the meat, the meat should fall apart quite easily. and will appear shredded. You may brown the meat further if desired.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
('50ea1ba4-f94d-535f-a61d-0566a8e58906','d1dac293-8467-53df-b455-3c3469bf23cd',4,'Check seasoning then serve with polenta or the more traditional thick cornmeal porridge known as pap or sadza, and a side of green vegetables.',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00',timestamp with time zone '2026-10-03 08:00:00+00','themealdb-import','themealdb-import',0),
